{"title":"ENVE’s $125 Tubeless Tape Gun Is Basically Gift Wrap for Your Rims","link":"https://bikerumor.com/enve-tubeless-tape-gun-review/","date":1794513910000,"content":"<p><img src=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/ENVE-Tubeless-Tape-Gun-review-package--1536x1152.jpeg\" width=\"1536\" height=\"1152\" alt=\"ENVE Tubeless Tape Gun review package\" /></p>\n<p><strong><em>I feel like this announcement should start like an infomercial or one of those “As Seen on TV” things.</em></strong> <em>“Are you tired of tubeless tape wrecking your day? (house starts on fire) Are your hands too greasy to get proper adhesion to the rim? (drops expensive wheel</em>, <em>blows up) Are you also fanatical about properly wrapped gifts? Well, boy, do we have a gadget for you!” </em></p>\n\n\n\n<figure><a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/ENVE-Tubeless-Tape-Gun-review-tool-solo-scaled.jpeg\"><img width=\"2560\" height=\"1440\" src=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/ENVE-Tubeless-Tape-Gun-review-tool-solo-scaled.jpeg\" alt=\"ENVE Tubeless Tape Gun review tool solo\" srcset=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/ENVE-Tubeless-Tape-Gun-review-tool-solo-scaled.jpeg 2560w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/ENVE-Tubeless-Tape-Gun-review-tool-solo-297x167.jpeg 297w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/ENVE-Tubeless-Tape-Gun-review-tool-solo-1536x864.jpeg 1536w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/ENVE-Tubeless-Tape-Gun-review-tool-solo-120x68.jpeg 120w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/ENVE-Tubeless-Tape-Gun-review-tool-solo-768x432.jpeg 768w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/ENVE-Tubeless-Tape-Gun-review-tool-solo-2048x1152.jpeg 2048w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/ENVE-Tubeless-Tape-Gun-review-tool-solo-1200x675.jpeg 1200w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/ENVE-Tubeless-Tape-Gun-review-tool-solo-1600x900.jpeg 1600w\" /></a><figcaption>For full instructions with video guidance, scan the QR code. (Photo/Jordan Villella)</figcaption></figure>\n\n\n\n<p>ENVE’s new Tubeless Tape Gun is exactly what it sounds like: a dedicated shop tool for installing tubeless rim tape quickly, straight, and with consistent tension. It looks a little like someone crossed a label maker with a caulking gun, and at $125, it costs considerably more than the roll of tape you’ll be feeding through it.</p>\n\n\n\n<p><strong><em>BUT before you judge </em></strong>– I’ve used it, and it’s pretty fantastic. It works as advertised, plus it looks cool, but that doesn’t mean we’re gonna stop joking around. Because it’s fun, and ENVE knows how to take a joke. And, annoyingly for anyone hoping this would be easy to make fun of, it works really well.</p>\n\n\n\n<figure><a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/ENVE-Tubeless-Tape-Gun-review-tool-details--scaled.jpeg\"><img width=\"2560\" height=\"1440\" src=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/ENVE-Tubeless-Tape-Gun-review-tool-details--scaled.jpeg\" alt=\"ENVE Tubeless Tape Gun review tool details\" srcset=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/ENVE-Tubeless-Tape-Gun-review-tool-details--scaled.jpeg 2560w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/ENVE-Tubeless-Tape-Gun-review-tool-details--297x167.jpeg 297w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/ENVE-Tubeless-Tape-Gun-review-tool-details--1536x864.jpeg 1536w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/ENVE-Tubeless-Tape-Gun-review-tool-details--120x68.jpeg 120w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/ENVE-Tubeless-Tape-Gun-review-tool-details--768x432.jpeg 768w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/ENVE-Tubeless-Tape-Gun-review-tool-details--2048x1152.jpeg 2048w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/ENVE-Tubeless-Tape-Gun-review-tool-details--1200x675.jpeg 1200w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/ENVE-Tubeless-Tape-Gun-review-tool-details--1600x900.jpeg 1600w\" /></a><figcaption>(Photo/Jordan Villella)</figcaption></figure>\n\n\n\n<h1>ENVE Tubeless Tape Gun</h1>\n\n\n\n<p>Installing tubeless tape isn’t difficult, but doing it cleanly can be a pain. On a new set of wheels, it’s more of a practice in patience.<em> “Don’t mess up the customer’s new wheelset with a big ol’ crinkle in the tape.” </em>It’s more of an annoying task on a well-used wheel, mostly because it means something isn’t working/sealing correctly. </p>\n\n\n\n<figure>\n<figure><a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/ENVE-Tubeless-Tape-Gun-review-need-new-rim-tape--scaled.jpeg\"><img width=\"1536\" height=\"1152\" src=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/ENVE-Tubeless-Tape-Gun-review-need-new-rim-tape--1536x1152.jpeg\" alt=\"ENVE Tubeless Tape Gun review need new rim tape\" srcset=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/ENVE-Tubeless-Tape-Gun-review-need-new-rim-tape--1536x1152.jpeg 1536w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/ENVE-Tubeless-Tape-Gun-review-need-new-rim-tape--297x223.jpeg 297w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/ENVE-Tubeless-Tape-Gun-review-need-new-rim-tape--120x90.jpeg 120w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/ENVE-Tubeless-Tape-Gun-review-need-new-rim-tape--768x576.jpeg 768w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/ENVE-Tubeless-Tape-Gun-review-need-new-rim-tape--2048x1536.jpeg 2048w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/ENVE-Tubeless-Tape-Gun-review-need-new-rim-tape--1200x900.jpeg 1200w\" /></a></figure>\n\n\n\n<figure><a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/ENVE-Tubeless-Tape-Gun-review-bag-rim-tape--scaled.jpeg\"><img width=\"1536\" height=\"864\" src=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/ENVE-Tubeless-Tape-Gun-review-bag-rim-tape--1536x864.jpeg\" alt=\"ENVE Tubeless Tape Gun review bag rim tape\" srcset=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/ENVE-Tubeless-Tape-Gun-review-bag-rim-tape--1536x864.jpeg 1536w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/ENVE-Tubeless-Tape-Gun-review-bag-rim-tape--297x167.jpeg 297w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/ENVE-Tubeless-Tape-Gun-review-bag-rim-tape--120x68.jpeg 120w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/ENVE-Tubeless-Tape-Gun-review-bag-rim-tape--768x432.jpeg 768w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/ENVE-Tubeless-Tape-Gun-review-bag-rim-tape--2048x1152.jpeg 2048w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/ENVE-Tubeless-Tape-Gun-review-bag-rim-tape--1200x675.jpeg 1200w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/ENVE-Tubeless-Tape-Gun-review-bag-rim-tape--1600x900.jpeg 1600w\" /></a></figure>\n</figure>\n\n\n\n<p>When you’re re-tapping a rim, things can get messy, not only from cleaning the used rim, but from the taping process. You’re trying to keep the tape centered while maintaining tension, rotating the wheel, avoiding wrinkles, and making sure you don’t wander up the sidewall halfway around the rim.</p>\n\n\n\n<figure><a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/ENVE-Tubeless-Tape-Gun-review-c-tool-scaled.jpeg\"><img width=\"2560\" height=\"1920\" src=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/ENVE-Tubeless-Tape-Gun-review-c-tool-scaled.jpeg\" alt=\"ENVE Tubeless Tape Gun review c tool\" srcset=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/ENVE-Tubeless-Tape-Gun-review-c-tool-scaled.jpeg 2560w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/ENVE-Tubeless-Tape-Gun-review-c-tool-297x223.jpeg 297w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/ENVE-Tubeless-Tape-Gun-review-c-tool-1536x1152.jpeg 1536w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/ENVE-Tubeless-Tape-Gun-review-c-tool-120x90.jpeg 120w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/ENVE-Tubeless-Tape-Gun-review-c-tool-768x576.jpeg 768w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/ENVE-Tubeless-Tape-Gun-review-c-tool-2048x1536.jpeg 2048w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/ENVE-Tubeless-Tape-Gun-review-c-tool-1200x900.jpeg 1200w\" /></a><figcaption>Looks like it came from ULINE, but one from an alternate universe. (Photo/Jordan Villella)</figcaption></figure>\n\n\n\n<p>If you’ve worked in a shop, you can do it easily, but wouldn’t it be cool to have a tool for it? The ENVE Tape Gun just makes the process cleaner and more repeatable, especially for first-timers.</p>\n\n\n\n<p><strong><em>How Does it Work?</em></strong> A shaped roller centers the tape in the rim bed while you push the tool forward and rotate the wheel toward you. A thin rear wheel pushes the tape down onto the center of the rim bed. Once you finish the lap, a built-in metal cutting blade trims the tape without reaching for scissors or a knife.</p>\n\n\n\n<figure><a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/ENVE-Tubeless-Tape-Gun-review-back-side-tool--scaled.jpeg\"><img width=\"2560\" height=\"1440\" src=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/ENVE-Tubeless-Tape-Gun-review-back-side-tool--scaled.jpeg\" alt=\"ENVE Tubeless Tape Gun review back side tool\" srcset=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/ENVE-Tubeless-Tape-Gun-review-back-side-tool--scaled.jpeg 2560w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/ENVE-Tubeless-Tape-Gun-review-back-side-tool--297x167.jpeg 297w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/ENVE-Tubeless-Tape-Gun-review-back-side-tool--1536x864.jpeg 1536w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/ENVE-Tubeless-Tape-Gun-review-back-side-tool--120x68.jpeg 120w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/ENVE-Tubeless-Tape-Gun-review-back-side-tool--768x432.jpeg 768w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/ENVE-Tubeless-Tape-Gun-review-back-side-tool--2048x1152.jpeg 2048w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/ENVE-Tubeless-Tape-Gun-review-back-side-tool--1200x675.jpeg 1200w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/ENVE-Tubeless-Tape-Gun-review-back-side-tool--1600x900.jpeg 1600w\" /></a><figcaption>(Photo/Jordan Villella)</figcaption></figure>\n\n\n\n<p>I like to think of it as one of those fancy wrapping-paper cutters you see around the holidays, except this one is made of aluminum and costs enough that your family might think you have issues.</p>\n\n\n\n<figure><a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/ENVE-Tubeless-Tape-Gun-review-weight--scaled.jpeg\"><img width=\"2560\" height=\"1920\" src=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/ENVE-Tubeless-Tape-Gun-review-weight--scaled.jpeg\" alt=\"ENVE Tubeless Tape Gun review weight\" srcset=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/ENVE-Tubeless-Tape-Gun-review-weight--scaled.jpeg 2560w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/ENVE-Tubeless-Tape-Gun-review-weight--297x223.jpeg 297w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/ENVE-Tubeless-Tape-Gun-review-weight--1536x1152.jpeg 1536w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/ENVE-Tubeless-Tape-Gun-review-weight--120x90.jpeg 120w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/ENVE-Tubeless-Tape-Gun-review-weight--768x576.jpeg 768w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/ENVE-Tubeless-Tape-Gun-review-weight--2048x1536.jpeg 2048w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/ENVE-Tubeless-Tape-Gun-review-weight--1200x900.jpeg 1200w\" /></a><figcaption>(Photo/Jordan Villella)</figcaption></figure>\n\n\n\n<h3>Built Like a Shop Tool</h3>\n\n\n\n<p>The first thing that stood out when I used the ENVE Tape Gun was how solid it feels. This isn’t a lightweight plastic tape dispenser.</p>\n\n\n\n<p>ENVE uses an aluminum skeleton, rubber grip, durable plastic guides, and a metal cutting blade (also replaceable). It feels built to survive a busy service department rather than sit at the bottom of a home toolbox.</p>\n\n\n\n<figure><a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/ENVE-Tubeless-Tape-Gun-review-size-options--scaled.jpeg\"><img width=\"2560\" height=\"1440\" src=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/ENVE-Tubeless-Tape-Gun-review-size-options--scaled.jpeg\" alt=\"ENVE Tubeless Tape Gun review size options\" srcset=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/ENVE-Tubeless-Tape-Gun-review-size-options--scaled.jpeg 2560w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/ENVE-Tubeless-Tape-Gun-review-size-options--297x167.jpeg 297w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/ENVE-Tubeless-Tape-Gun-review-size-options--1536x864.jpeg 1536w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/ENVE-Tubeless-Tape-Gun-review-size-options--120x68.jpeg 120w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/ENVE-Tubeless-Tape-Gun-review-size-options--768x432.jpeg 768w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/ENVE-Tubeless-Tape-Gun-review-size-options--2048x1152.jpeg 2048w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/ENVE-Tubeless-Tape-Gun-review-size-options--1200x675.jpeg 1200w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/ENVE-Tubeless-Tape-Gun-review-size-options--1600x900.jpeg 1600w\" /></a><figcaption>(Photo/Jordan Villella)</figcaption></figure>\n\n\n\n<p>The ENVE Tape Gun works with rolls using a 75mm / 3-inch core and accepts tape widths from 25mm to 40mm, which covers a broad range of road, gravel, and mountain bike rims.</p>\n\n\n\n<figure><a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/ENVE-Tubeless-Tape-Gun-review-in-use--scaled.jpg\"><img width=\"2560\" height=\"1707\" src=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/ENVE-Tubeless-Tape-Gun-review-in-use--scaled.jpg\" alt=\"ENVE Tubeless Tape Gun review in use\" srcset=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/ENVE-Tubeless-Tape-Gun-review-in-use--scaled.jpg 2560w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/ENVE-Tubeless-Tape-Gun-review-in-use--297x198.jpg 297w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/ENVE-Tubeless-Tape-Gun-review-in-use--1536x1024.jpg 1536w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/ENVE-Tubeless-Tape-Gun-review-in-use--120x80.jpg 120w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/ENVE-Tubeless-Tape-Gun-review-in-use--768x512.jpg 768w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/ENVE-Tubeless-Tape-Gun-review-in-use--2048x1365.jpg 2048w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/ENVE-Tubeless-Tape-Gun-review-in-use--800x533.jpg 800w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/ENVE-Tubeless-Tape-Gun-review-in-use--720x480.jpg 720w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/ENVE-Tubeless-Tape-Gun-review-in-use--1350x900.jpg 1350w\" /></a><figcaption>(Photo/ENVE)</figcaption></figure>\n\n\n\n<h3>Really….Does It Actually Work?</h3>\n\n\n\n<p>Yes, and damn well. The Tape Gun keeps the tape centered, maintains good tension, and makes the entire process feel much more controlled and, dare I say, easy.</p>\n\n\n\n<figure><a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/ENVE-Tubeless-Tape-Gun-review-measure-your-old-tape--scaled.jpeg\"><img width=\"2560\" height=\"1920\" src=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/ENVE-Tubeless-Tape-Gun-review-measure-your-old-tape--scaled.jpeg\" alt=\"ENVE Tubeless Tape Gun review measure your old tape\" srcset=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/ENVE-Tubeless-Tape-Gun-review-measure-your-old-tape--scaled.jpeg 2560w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/ENVE-Tubeless-Tape-Gun-review-measure-your-old-tape--297x223.jpeg 297w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/ENVE-Tubeless-Tape-Gun-review-measure-your-old-tape--1536x1152.jpeg 1536w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/ENVE-Tubeless-Tape-Gun-review-measure-your-old-tape--120x90.jpeg 120w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/ENVE-Tubeless-Tape-Gun-review-measure-your-old-tape--768x576.jpeg 768w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/ENVE-Tubeless-Tape-Gun-review-measure-your-old-tape--2048x1536.jpeg 2048w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/ENVE-Tubeless-Tape-Gun-review-measure-your-old-tape--1200x900.jpeg 1200w\" /></a><figcaption>(Photo/Jordan Villella)</figcaption></figure>\n\n\n\n<p>For a tryout, I retaped my cyclocross wheels that badly needed a refresh. The tubeless tape was starting to dip at the edges (those not-so-flattering images above) and pull up where the tape overlapped. </p>\n\n\n\n<p>The process was simple: I pulled off the old tape, cleaned the rim, and measured the old tape. It came in at 25mm, so I used the ENVE tape designed for 29mm (fitting rim inner width from 24-26mm)</p>\n\n\n\n<p><strong><em>What did I notice? </em></strong><em>The biggest improvement is consistency; </em>you’re not trying to do four things at once, you’re just rotating the wheel and steering the tape.</p>\n\n\n\n<figure><a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/ENVE-Tubeless-Tape-Gun-review-demo-without-tape--scaled.jpeg\"><img width=\"2560\" height=\"1920\" src=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/ENVE-Tubeless-Tape-Gun-review-demo-without-tape--scaled.jpeg\" alt=\"ENVE Tubeless Tape Gun review demo without tape\" srcset=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/ENVE-Tubeless-Tape-Gun-review-demo-without-tape--scaled.jpeg 2560w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/ENVE-Tubeless-Tape-Gun-review-demo-without-tape--297x223.jpeg 297w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/ENVE-Tubeless-Tape-Gun-review-demo-without-tape--1536x1152.jpeg 1536w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/ENVE-Tubeless-Tape-Gun-review-demo-without-tape--120x90.jpeg 120w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/ENVE-Tubeless-Tape-Gun-review-demo-without-tape--768x576.jpeg 768w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/ENVE-Tubeless-Tape-Gun-review-demo-without-tape--2048x1536.jpeg 2048w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/ENVE-Tubeless-Tape-Gun-review-demo-without-tape--1200x900.jpeg 1200w\" /></a><figcaption>Getting used to the steering on the tape gun takes a sec, so don’t start speed taping from the gun. (Photo/Jordan Villella)</figcaption></figure>\n\n\n\n<p>When you’re taping wheels by hand, the first one usually looks perfect. If you’re doing more than a set, thats when things can go downhill. By wheel number six, you start negotiating with yourself about whether being 2mm off-center really matters. Then you wonder whether to trim with a razor (no) or try again.</p>\n\n\n\n<figure><a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/ENVE-Tubeless-Tape-Gun-review-instructions--scaled.jpeg\"><img width=\"2560\" height=\"1920\" src=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/ENVE-Tubeless-Tape-Gun-review-instructions--scaled.jpeg\" alt=\"ENVE Tubeless Tape Gun review instructions\" srcset=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/ENVE-Tubeless-Tape-Gun-review-instructions--scaled.jpeg 2560w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/ENVE-Tubeless-Tape-Gun-review-instructions--297x223.jpeg 297w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/ENVE-Tubeless-Tape-Gun-review-instructions--1536x1152.jpeg 1536w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/ENVE-Tubeless-Tape-Gun-review-instructions--120x90.jpeg 120w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/ENVE-Tubeless-Tape-Gun-review-instructions--768x576.jpeg 768w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/ENVE-Tubeless-Tape-Gun-review-instructions--2048x1536.jpeg 2048w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/ENVE-Tubeless-Tape-Gun-review-instructions--1200x900.jpeg 1200w\" /></a><figcaption>(Photo/Jordan Villella)</figcaption></figure>\n\n\n\n<p><strong><em>With the ENVE Tape Gun, the process is basically the same every time.</em></strong></p>\n\n\n\n<ol>\n<li>Install the tape you need for the rim width.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Attach the tape to the rim.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Push the tool.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Rotate the wheel.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>“Wheelie” to cut the tape.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Done.</li>\n</ol>\n\n\n\n<p>For a professional shop, race mechanic, wheel builder, or anyone regularly setting up tubeless wheels, that repeatability is genuinely useful.</p>\n\n\n\n<p>It also makes the finished job look better, and anyone who’s had to troubleshoot a slow tubeless leak knows neat tape installation isn’t purely cosmetic.</p>\n\n\n\n<figure><a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/ENVE-Tubeless-Tape-Gun-review-header--scaled.jpeg\"><img width=\"2560\" height=\"1440\" src=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/ENVE-Tubeless-Tape-Gun-review-header--scaled.jpeg\" alt=\"ENVE Tubeless Tape Gun review header\" srcset=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/ENVE-Tubeless-Tape-Gun-review-header--scaled.jpeg 2560w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/ENVE-Tubeless-Tape-Gun-review-header--297x167.jpeg 297w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/ENVE-Tubeless-Tape-Gun-review-header--1536x864.jpeg 1536w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/ENVE-Tubeless-Tape-Gun-review-header--120x67.jpeg 120w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/ENVE-Tubeless-Tape-Gun-review-header--768x432.jpeg 768w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/ENVE-Tubeless-Tape-Gun-review-header--2048x1152.jpeg 2048w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/ENVE-Tubeless-Tape-Gun-review-header--1200x675.jpeg 1200w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/ENVE-Tubeless-Tape-Gun-review-header--1600x900.jpeg 1600w\" /></a><figcaption>(Photo/Jordan Villella)</figcaption></figure>\n\n\n\n<h3>But… $125?</h3>\n\n\n\n<p>Here’s the problem. It’s $125. If you tape two wheels a year in your garage, there’s almost no way to make the math work. A thumb still costs considerably less.</p>\n\n\n\n<p>For a home mechanic, this lands squarely in the category of <em>“extremely nice tool that you absolutely do not need.”</em></p>\n\n\n\n<figure><a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/ENVE-Tubeless-Tape-Gun-review-tool-wheels--scaled.jpeg\"><img width=\"2560\" height=\"1920\" src=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/ENVE-Tubeless-Tape-Gun-review-tool-wheels--scaled.jpeg\" alt=\"ENVE Tubeless Tape Gun review tool wheels\" srcset=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/ENVE-Tubeless-Tape-Gun-review-tool-wheels--scaled.jpeg 2560w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/ENVE-Tubeless-Tape-Gun-review-tool-wheels--297x223.jpeg 297w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/ENVE-Tubeless-Tape-Gun-review-tool-wheels--1536x1152.jpeg 1536w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/ENVE-Tubeless-Tape-Gun-review-tool-wheels--120x90.jpeg 120w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/ENVE-Tubeless-Tape-Gun-review-tool-wheels--768x576.jpeg 768w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/ENVE-Tubeless-Tape-Gun-review-tool-wheels--2048x1536.jpeg 2048w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/ENVE-Tubeless-Tape-Gun-review-tool-wheels--1200x900.jpeg 1200w\" /></a><figcaption>The ENVE Tape Gun is built like a beast, and most pieces are serviceable. (Photo/Jordan Villella)</figcaption></figure>\n\n\n\n<p>For a shop, though, the argument gets easier. If you’re setting up tubeless tires every day, saving a little time and getting more consistent results adds up. The Tape Gun also feels built well enough that I’d expect it to survive years of normal shop use. Plus, if you’re an ENVE dealer, it’s a cool tool to have out and chat with customers about.</p>\n\n\n\n<p>That’s probably where ENVE nailed the product. It’s cool-looking and works. It doesn’t solve a complicated problem. It just makes a repetitive job faster and cleaner. </p>\n\n\n\n<figure><a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/ENVE-Tubeless-Tape-Gun-review-rolling--scaled.jpg\"><img width=\"2560\" height=\"1707\" src=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/ENVE-Tubeless-Tape-Gun-review-rolling--scaled.jpg\" alt=\"ENVE Tubeless Tape Gun review rolling\" srcset=\"https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/ENVE-Tubeless-Tape-Gun-review-rolling--scaled.jpg 2560w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/ENVE-Tubeless-Tape-Gun-review-rolling--297x198.jpg 297w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/ENVE-Tubeless-Tape-Gun-review-rolling--1536x1024.jpg 1536w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/ENVE-Tubeless-Tape-Gun-review-rolling--120x80.jpg 120w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/ENVE-Tubeless-Tape-Gun-review-rolling--768x512.jpg 768w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/ENVE-Tubeless-Tape-Gun-review-rolling--2048x1365.jpg 2048w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/ENVE-Tubeless-Tape-Gun-review-rolling--800x533.jpg 800w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/ENVE-Tubeless-Tape-Gun-review-rolling--720x480.jpg 720w, https://bikerumor.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/ENVE-Tubeless-Tape-Gun-review-rolling--1350x900.jpg 1350w\" /></a><figcaption>Did we mention it’s the same one they use at the ENVE HQ in Ogden, Utah? Because it is. (Photo/ENVE)</figcaption></figure>\n\n\n\n<h3>The Perfect Gift for the Mechanic Who Has Everything?</h3>\n\n\n\n<p>This might also be one of <a href=\"https://bikerumor.com/best-gifts-for-bike-mechanics-people-who-work-on-bicycles/\">the most oddly appropriate mechanic gifts of the holiday season.</a></p>\n\n\n\n<p>You could wrap the Tape Gun, then they can unwrap it and use it to wrap wheels. </p>\n\n\n\n<p><strong><em>There’s some nice symmetry there.</em></strong></p>\n\n\n\n<p>Jokes aside, the ENVE Tubeless Tape Gun is a genuinely excellent tool. It works exactly as advertised, feels properly shop-grade, and takes some of the annoyance out of one of the least exciting parts of a tubeless setup.</p>\n\n\n\n<p>Do most riders need one? Absolutely not.</p>\n\n\n\n<p><em>Would I happily use one every time I tape a wheel? <a href=\"https://enve.com/products/tubeless-tape-gun\">Yep. That’s the problem with nice tools.</a></em></p>","author":"Jordan Villella","comments":"https://bikerumor.com/enve-tubeless-tape-gun-review/#comments","siteTitle":"Bikerumor","siteHash":"49f427af0a926f4232eb837006841d7242e153e3afbb590f32e4b104ea3e2718","entryHash":"483c8148d842d520b42ca15e160035796e36d51fad92790eb45ffdda739d5a69","category":"Cycling"}